The wind grows still. I look up to see Adva, stiff and injured. She looks at my eyes, but her gaze shoots through me. “... You’re alive.” She says softly, her voice cracking. 

I stand with her assistance, leaning on her. Her face is soaked in her own tears and blood. “Where’s Kael?” 

I shake my head, the sheer thought of having to utter the truth causing me to weep harder. Adva hugs me, holding me close. I see Xor's lifeless body laying in the far distance. There’s no flames, no toxins— just
the snow flying around, stirred by the air. 

We are now all alone in this world. No guide, no safety, no home. The world is hostile to us. What’s standing in front of me is all I have, and she’s equally as clueless as I. The cold wind of this continent
stings against my skin.

Adva asks the question I never wanted to consider. “What now?”

I stare, thinking deeply. This world betrayed us when we did little beyond fight to keep our identity. This world tried to subjugate us to nothing more than tools. This world murdered the one and only human 
who treated us like equals. They want to be afraid of us so bad, I can give them a reason to be afraid. 

“Revenge.” I utter softly through my tears. “For Amei. For Kael.” 
